Hmm wait — actually is that right? CRAP = CC²×(1−cov)³ + CC. At cov=1.0: CC. Yes. So any method with CC > 12 exceeds the threshold even fully covered. The baseline comment says "83 at 9.00 (CC-9 @ 100%)". So indeed fully-covered methods read CRAP = CC. CC 17 fails.

